# TrainGrid environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit real values:
# .env, .env.local and every other .env.* file are ignored by Git.
#
# Local development points at the local Supabase stack (npm run supabase:start),
# never at the production project. Production values live only in
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production).

# --- Public: sent to the browser by design -----------------------------------
# Safety comes from Supabase Auth and Row Level Security, not from hiding these.

# Local stack: http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# Publishable key (starts with sb_publishable_). For the local stack, copy it
# from the output of: npm run supabase:status
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key

# --- Server only: must never reach the browser --------------------------------
# In production these are set in Vercel only (Production environment).
# Locally, use the secret key of the local stack (npm run supabase:status);
# the admin page and the E2E tests that need it skip or stay disabled without it.

# Secret key (starts with sb_secret_). Bypasses Row Level Security.
# Used only by the admin invitation page, after the caller is confirmed as admin.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Comma-separated Supabase user ids (UUIDs) allowed to manage invitations.
# Find yours in Supabase → Authentication → Users.
# TRAINGRID_ADMIN_USER_IDS=

# --- Site and time zone (server only) ----------------------------------------

# Public origin of this deployment, e.g. https://train-grid.vercel.app. Used for
# the sign-in link in invitation emails, absolute metadata URLs and the
# canonical link of /. Plain http is accepted only for localhost/127.0.0.1.
# Without it, Vercel's VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL is used.
# TRAINGRID_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# IANA zone used for "today" until the browser reports its own (tg_tz cookie).
# TRAINGRID_DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE=Australia/Sydney

# --- Invitation email (server only; see docs/EMAIL_SETUP.md) -----------------
# Without these, invitations still work and no email is sent.

# Resend API key with sending access (starts with re_). Never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Sender on a domain verified in Resend.
# TRAINGRID_EMAIL_FROM=TrainGrid <invites@mail.yourdomain.com>
# Optional reply-to address.
# TRAINGRID_EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
